A||||12||Alex4mula||My 3.4 recipe & 1st test drive!!||||10||
Z||000000||Alex4mula||06-06-2000||09:57 AM||||PARTS:<BR>Car: <BR> 88 Formula 5 speed<P>Clutch: <BR> Fieroshop full Kevlar clutch<P>Engine: <BR> Grooms remanufactured 3.4 modified by Ed Parks @ Fiero Factory<P>Go fast parts added:<BR>- FOCOA headers coated<BR>- Under drive pulley<BR>- Ported all intake manifolds<BR>- Ported throttle body and plenum<BR>- K&N filter<BR>- Jacobs wires and computer<BR>- Hypertech stage III chip with 160 deg thermostat<BR>- No CC<P>Fuel system:<BR>- Stock 2.8 injectors<BR>- Adjustable Fuel pressure regulator<P>Other:<BR>- New engine mounts<BR>- Poly dog bone<BR>- New O2 sensor<BR>- New belts<BR>- New fuel filter<BR>- Stock AC Delco plugs (.060 gap)<P>Installation:<BR> Everything was almost straight forward. Waiting for headers (7 wks) had time to clean and paint everything. Cradle was dropped and all except upper intake & A/C was installed at that time. Headers quality & fit is excellent. I don't see any other way of installing them than with the cradle outside unless you like real pain. Ed provided me a front mount bracket that was useless. For some reason it was misalign one inch away of mount screws. I discovered that you can use the 88 bracket by just cutting away the top left bolt hole area. Not hard at all. It is necessary because the 3.4 use in that area a pre 88 shock mount bracket to mount a pre 88 A/C bracket. The 88 A/C bracket front hole moves near 1/2 inch  inward and does not align. 88 oil pan, timing covers and flywheel was used. With the engine back in place the headers cleared everything nicely. Ported TBS & plenum done by Darrel Morse. Great quality & better price.<P>Test drive:<BR> Fieroshop clutch feels excellent. As smooth or better than a Centerforce that I used to have. No chatter at all. Very smooth. Flywheel was resurfaced. Hard launches not tested due to break-in period (Aaghh!!!). The engine…. WOW!! Sound is definitely different. 3.4 is quieter than the 2.8 even with the headers. I still have the stock muffler without cat. It feels real quick. Especially from 2500 to 3800 it starts pulling real hard. Haven't gone farther because of break-in but I bet it will pull all the way to 6000 or 6500. Haven't adjusted fuel yet. Will check later at WOT with scanner for lean condition. Now it runs good. Plan on dyno it later (1-2 mo) & post results.<BR>Well sorry for the long post but I don't have a web page & wanted to share this. Thanks all for this forum which guided me to all the info required for me to accomplish this conversion. Questions welcome.<P>Alex3.4mula!!<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000001||fiero56||06-06-2000||10:38 AM||||Reading your post, makes me want to get my 3.4 project underway sooner.<P>What kind of total cost are we looking at here? How about just for the engine, and everything Ed takes care of? I can't wait to put one in my Formula.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Raydar||06-06-2000||10:40 AM||||Alex, Congrats on your success! <BR>This is something I hope to do in the not too distant future, so I may take you up on your offer to answer questions. <BR>Since your engine was a reman, was it still a 3.4, or was it bored enough to make it a 3.5? <BR>In any event... WAY TA' GO!!!||||reg||14
Z||000003||Alex4mula||06-06-2000||11:32 AM||||Engine sure must be more than 3.4 ltrs due to reman process. How much more I did not ask. Ed should know. In terms of cost these are the main ones with suppliers:<P>3.4 engine: $1725 + $450 mods & brackets -Fiero Factory<P>Headers: $730 with coating -FOCOA<P>Pulley/FP reg/mounts/Gaskets/Misc: $400 - Fiero Store & Auto parts stores<P>Ported TBS/Plenum to match: $150 - Darrel Morse<P>Wires: $65 - Jacobs Electronics (had computer & Accel coil already)<P>Labor: $$$$$$$ Myself alone.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||fierosound||06-06-2000||02:42 PM||||Alex...<P>What CAMSHAFT is in this engine??  Usually the cam and heads mod are the most important factors for producing power.||||reg||1
