Z||000006||Alex4mula||06-06-2000||03:45 PM||||As far as I know this are the specs:<BR>Camshaft  Lift: .427" Int., .454" Exh.<BR>Camshaft Duration @ .050"........204° Int., 216° Exh.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Alex4mula||06-06-2000||04:29 PM||||Why should I go to 180 thermo instead of the 160? I have the 160 because is required by the Hypertech chip.||||reg||1
Z||000008||87PegasusGT||06-07-2000||03:42 PM||||180 Degree runs very cool. 160 keeps it running rich becaue it doesn't run hot enough. What is the Hypertech Stage 3? I have a drag 2.8 Prom and am swapping it for a special 3.4 PROM. (Camaro one won't work)||||reg||1
Z||000009||Alex4mula||06-07-2000||04:04 PM||||Back about 10 years ago Hypertech use to have three chips (Stage I, II & III) for the Fiero. As far as I remember it was something like this; Stage I just messed up with the TC on automatics, Stage II added changing the spark curve and the Stage III was an offroad one which also added a disabled EGR, required a 160 deg thermo and elimination of cat.||||reg||1
Z||000010||87PegasusGT||06-07-2000||06:16 PM||||Ah... probably like the drag PROM I got (for offroad use only). I still think the the custom one for the 3.4 in a Fiero will work better.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Alex4mula||06-08-2000||09:43 AM||||Later on I plan to add a supercharger. Will need a custom PROM then.||||reg||1
Z||000012||terryk||06-09-2000||12:20 AM||||I looked at one of the early Thprecyhpc Egats I chips and found all of the changes were in areas where it didn't matter. Other than some minor spark changes at low RPM's, the rest of the changes were in the -40 to 8F coolant range. For an 85 V6. Well, at least they removed the speed limiter and raised the rev limiter.<P>But boy, until the coolant hit 8 degrees F, the car ran like an animal! ||||reg||11
